{"schema_version": 2, "run_id": "analytics-construction-posture-fix-round", "commit_range": "24057d6ed..a314c5f22 (scoped to b62d9ebad+a314c5f22 hand-authored content)", "reporter": "cpp-safety", "recorded_by": null, "source": "governance-agent", "reporter_ref": null, "reviewed_at_sha": "a314c5f22", "recorded_at": "2026-08-19T23:00:00Z", "pass_ordinal": 1, "finding_id": "an-safety-1", "severity_native": "BLOCKING", "severity_mapped": "BLOCKING", "trigger": "SIGTERM/SIGINT delivered to a non-main thread while server has live gateway-forward traffic", "impact": ["I5"], "exposure": ["E0", "E5"], "epistemic_status": "likely", "independent_reporters": 1, "policy_floor": "ownership/lifetime defect (UAF-class) per cpp-safety blocking contract -- contested, see adjudication", "provenance": "pre-existing (narrower reorder-order delta); underlying #3279 race pre-existing", "file": "server/core/src/server.cpp", "line": "7480-7513 (pre-fix)", "summary": "Claimed the merge's teardown order moves analytics_store_'s destruction earlier relative to the SQLite predecessor's implicit post-stop() destruction, worsening #3279 exposure. Orchestrator-verified: ~ServerImpl(){stop();} means during-stop() and right-after-stop()-returns are the same moment, undermining the specific 'moved to during stop()' framing. architect independently found the REAL, narrower delta (teardown ORDER among sibling blocks, not stop()-vs-destructor timing) and graded it SHOULD. security-guardian/sre/cpp-expert did not derive BLOCKING. Resolved via Gate 7 fix: reordered analytics_store_.reset() to occur LAST among the sibling teardown blocks (just before pg_pool_.reset()), restoring the predecessor's effective end-of-stop() free-point. Gate 8 cpp-safety re-review to confirm disposition on the fixed code.", "classification": "n/a", "disposition": "deferred-to-issue #3279 (residual, post-reorder)", "adjudicated_by": "orchestrator (Claude), evidence-based re-derivation pending Gate 8 re-review", "adjudication_rationale": "The specific mechanism claimed (post-stop()-return implicit destruction happening meaningfully later than an explicit mid-stop() reset) does not hold: ~ServerImpl's entire body is `{ stop(); }`, so both happen at the same moment. The REAL, narrower delta -- teardown order among sibling blocks affecting exposure relative to the webhook/offload 60s quiesce -- is architect's finding, fixed via reorder. The underlying #3279 detached-thread race is pre-existing, already deferred by Dave for the sibling stores (commit 4c070b484), and not closed by this reorder -- only reduced.", "caused_by": null, "waiver_rationale": null, "refuted_by": null, "refuted_by_reporter": null}
